WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.532
I need the Department of Higher Education.

00:00:02.692 --> 00:00:03.609
Tab to About.

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:04.498
Down arrow.

00:00:04.658 --> 00:00:05.737
Where did the link go?

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.458
I turn on Curb Cut.

00:00:08.618 --> 00:00:09.429
Same menu.

00:00:09.589 --> 00:00:10.552
Same keyboard.

00:00:10.712 --> 00:00:11.409
There it is.

00:00:11.569 --> 00:00:12.435
The DHE.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.319
Kane tries the same task with a mouse.

00:00:17.479 --> 00:00:19.086
The department page opens.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.716
With keys alone, Kane cannot reach that link.

00:00:23.876 --> 00:00:25.833
Now we have a reproducible failure.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.132
Here’s a failure that went straight back to the coding agent.

00:00:30.292 --> 00:00:32.047
Watch the converter’s answer field.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.404
At this width, the field runs off the screen.

00:00:35.564 --> 00:00:39.975
Codex receives Kane’s failed assertion and writes a rule to stack the cells.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.322
Kane runs it again.

00:00:43.482 --> 00:00:44.217
One meter.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.590
The answer is visible.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:50.284
At Munich Airport, listen to the previous slide control.

00:00:50.444 --> 00:00:50.890
[Reading voice] Button.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.234
[Reading voice] Vorherige Folie.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.559
On Meridiano, two buttons have no names.

00:00:56.719 --> 00:00:59.068
TypeSafe Jev names them in about a second.

00:00:59.228 --> 00:00:59.584
[Reading voice] Menú.

00:00:59.744 --> 00:01:00.274
[Reading voice] Buscar.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.681
The site owner gets the task, the recordings, and a source repair.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.110
One hundred five fixes are live.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.632
Get Curb Cut for Chrome.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.094
How it works.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.638
On ExtremeTerrain, the Details link is faint.

00:01:21.798 --> 00:01:24.697
Curb Cut adjusts its contrast and measures the result.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:26.503
Kane does four jobs.

00:01:26.663 --> 00:01:32.155
It reproduces the barrier, runs the mouse control, verifies the fix, and checks it again later.

00:01:32.315 --> 00:01:33.790
Watch the date calculator.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.740
With a mouse, Kane adds two days.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.308
In Reading view, the field needs a name.

00:01:46.468 --> 00:01:48.103
The fix calls it Days to add.

00:01:48.263 --> 00:01:51.719
Kane finds that field, enters two, and selects Calculate.

00:01:51.879 --> 00:01:54.885
The recorded answer is Tuesday, November twenty-fourth.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:04.444
Run curbcut check.

00:02:04.604 --> 00:02:08.875
Kane tries the task and gives the coding agent the exact step that failed.

00:02:09.035 --> 00:02:10.404
The agent makes a change.

00:02:10.564 --> 00:02:11.583
Kane tries again.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:18.464
curbcut gate runs when the coding agent tries to stop.

00:02:18.624 --> 00:02:22.651
If the task still fails, the agent gets the failure and fixes the source.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.865
From the extension, open the proof for this fix.

00:02:29.025 --> 00:02:32.462
You can play the recording that earned its Kane verified status.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.883
Jev’s public test found names on seven sites.

00:02:37.043 --> 00:02:40.018
Thirteen of fifteen applied names were judged correct.

00:02:40.178 --> 00:02:41.160
Two were too vague.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:48.637
When another control stops you, one key opens a barrier report for that page.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.504
When the site works on its own, Curb Cut retires the fix.

00:02:54.664 --> 00:02:56.649
Everyone gets the repair from the source.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:00.602
Get Curb Cut for Chrome.

00:03:00.762 --> 00:03:01.796
Try the next key.
